<!--
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2024 Joinside <suitor-fall-life@duck.com>
  SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

  Auto Backup for Android 11 and below.

  Everything else may travel: the theme, the notification toggles and the Dualis cache all cost
  nothing to lose and nothing to leak. The credentials must not. Uninstalling takes them with it —
  and a backup that quietly carried them to the next install would undo exactly that.

  Excluding the file is also the only thing that works. EncryptedSharedPreferences is sealed with a
  key from the Android Keystore, and the Keystore is never backed up: a restored copy on another
  device is undecryptable bytes that the app has to detect and throw away.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="dualis_secure_prefs.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
